In recent years, 3D city models have become more prevalent within 

Problem was viewed from the perspective of a geo-engineer working on 3D city models and creating visualisation and running simulations. In order for him to efficiently collaborate with his team a Version Control System (VCS) is a necessity. Most 3D city models are written in CityGML or CityJSON format. In (paper stellios) implemented a draft version for a Versioning system for CityJSON files. 

The current version lacks the ability to detect geometries and is flawed for long time use. Internal storage gets loaded fast.













== Scientific Relevance

Eventhough CityGML offers a versioning option, but it is not used in the industry. CityJSON is a far more superior data format, in combination with the increasing amount of 3d City Models a need for reliable versioning module is there.